    // Manage the ACL of a document or folder on demand (ADR "Manage-access UI for document/folder ACLs").
    // The dialog is self-contained (loads the grants + picker, gates itself on the caller's CanManagePermissions).
    // A row carries its own address; the detail pane prefers the resource it already fetched, falling back to
    // the row's. Both end up handing the dialog ONE href to start from (ADR 0543, issue #416).
    //
    // `document` before `self` because a REPOSITORY row's `self` is the repository view, which is a different
    // resource with different rels — the document view is the one that carries the grants. A repository is a
    // document (ADR 0200), but only the server can say at which address, which is why it advertises both.

    private Task OpenManageAccessForSelectedAsync() =>
        Actions.OpenManageAccessAsync(
            _selectedItem!.Id,
            _sysName,
            _detailLinks?.GetValueOrDefault("self") ?? DocumentActions.DocumentAddress(_selectedItem!));


